'''Teeks''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that lived in [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Last Shot" /> At some point, a crashed [[Unidentified ark (Endor)|ark]] brought Teeks to the [[moon]] of [[Endor]].<ref name="BMF">{{BuildFalconCite|38|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> When [[Han Solo]] and [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] were searching for a [[pilot]] on [[Frander's Bay]], Solo pushed his way through a group of Teek before dodging a lumbering [[Kullp]].<ref name="Last Shot" /> A [[Unidentified dinghy driver|Teek]] worked at [[Borgo Prime|Port Borgo]] around [[9 ABY]].<ref name="Date">{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref><ref name="Skeleton">{{SkeletonCrew|Way, Way Out Past the Barrier}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Teek species made its live-action canon debut in "[[Way, Way Out Past the Barrier]]", the second episode of ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]''.<ref name="Skeleton" /> Director [[David Lowery]] used puppetry to bring the character to life.<ref name="Lowery">{{WebCite|url=https://www.empireonline.com/tv/news/star-wars-skeleton-crew-teek-ewok-battle-for-endor-exclusive|text=Star Wars: Skeleton Crew Will Bring Back The Teek From Ewok Movie The Battle For Endor|work=[[Wikipedia:Empire (magazine)|''Empire Online'']]|author=Travis, Ben|date=2024-10-21|archivedate=https://web.archive.org/web/20241119010144/https://www.empireonline.com/tv/news/star-wars-skeleton-crew-teek-ewok-battle-for-endor-exclusive/}}</ref>

